      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "Emgage Foundation demonstrates a neutral and balanced financial profile. Its <cite id=\"7\">93.3% program expense ratio</cite> is notably high, indicating that management and fundraising costs are covered by specific restricted funds or internal efficiencies. The organization is highly effective at resource acquisition, requiring only <cite id=\"7\">$0.01 in fundraising expenses for every dollar raised</cite>. This lean operation is supported by <cite id=\"7\">15.3 months of working capital</cite>, which provides a significant buffer against the <cite id=\"8\">recent 17% decline in annual revenue</cite>. Furthermore, the organization has achieved a <cite id=\"7\">perfect 100 score in the Leadership beacon</cite> from Charity Navigator, suggesting a stable governance structure despite having a <cite id=\"8\">relatively small board of three members</cite>."
      ],
      "summary": "Emgage Foundation operates as a national, non-partisan organization dedicated to mobilizing Muslim American voters through civic education and policy advocacy. The organization focuses on systemic change by increasing political participation within the community. In the most recent fiscal year, the foundation reported <cite id=\"8\">total revenue of $4,069,674</cite>, which represents a <cite id=\"8\">17% decline from the previous year's $4,918,661</cite>. Despite this revenue dip, the organization maintains a <cite id=\"7\">97/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite>, reflecting high standards of accountability. Their primary activities include the <cite id=\"3\">Million Muslim Votes Campaign</cite> and extensive <cite id=\"3\">Get Out The Vote (GOTV) programming</cite>. These efforts are designed to ensure Muslim American voices are represented in policy discussions. The foundation also invests in the next generation of leaders through its <cite id=\"3\">Emerging Leaders Program</cite>. While the organization does not provide direct humanitarian aid, it seeks to create impact by <cite id=\"7\">empowering over one million beneficiaries</cite> through civic engagement. This focus on long-term systemic influence distinguishes it from traditional relief charities.",
